  "notes": [
    "Preregistration baseline text incorrectly stated prior matched MGDA pooled +18.7576 bb/100. The hash-verified parent summary actually reports +0.5594 bb/100 CI half-width 16.3362; all final comparisons use the parent raw evaluation evidence directly, so the typo does not affect analysis."
  ],
  "result": {
    "summary": "CAGrad c=0.5 trained from the exact same 4,096 immutable hands, 9,026 decisions, 32 schedules, Standard10 initialization, and optimizer contract as the prior matched MGDA smoke, then completed 12,288 untouched internal evaluation games. All 32 CAGrad updates had positive worst-group alignment and median ordinary-direction cosine 0.9289, but CAGrad scored -3.9253 bb/100 versus ordinary and -4.4847 bb/100 versus exact matched MGDA, CI95 [-10.6941,+1.7247].",
    "conclusion": "CAGrad successfully fixes the geometric concern that MGDA can discard average-gradient progress, yet that cleaner geometry did not translate to matched outcome breadth: only one of three anchor differences was nonnegative and both seat differences were negative versus MGDA. Exact keys, decks, controls, logical schedules, source evidence, initialization, and anchor identities matched. This rejects c=0.5 under this residual/offline-update recipe; it does not reject all conflict-aware optimization or long-horizon learning, and no claim rests only on failure to beat Slumbot at small scale.",
    "decision": "REJECT_CAGRAD_C0P5_MATCHED_RECIPE_NO_65K",
    "next_step": "Do not scale this CAGrad recipe. Reassess alternatives that change the policy-improvement signal rather than only gradient aggregation—especially state-conditioned direct greedy improvement or opponent-adaptive recurrent self-play—while retaining geometric multi-seed curves, broad holdouts, both seats, Standard10 preservation, and external/proxy alignment as scale gates."
  },
